# NE-CREWAI-DROPIN — the CUSTOMER-SIDE CrewAI agent's isolated, hash-pinned venv.
#
# SOVEREIGNTY (the headline): NOTHING in this closure ever enters the platform
# uv.lock / SBOM / C4 license gate. crewai's BASE deps pull chromadb~=1.1.0, whose
# BASE deps pull posthog (its telemetry client) — and posthog is PERMANENTLY BARRED
# from the platform lock by a merge-blocking sovereignty guard
# (packages/ne-memory-graph/tests/test_no_graph_closure_in_lock.py) AND, redundantly,
# by this unit's packages/ne-mcp/tests/test_crewai_isolation.py. Beyond posthog the
# closure ALSO cannot resolve into the platform lock at all: four of crewai's tight
# base pins are in hard conflict with the locked platform (verified 2026-07-21):
#     crewai pydantic<2.13,>=2.11.9   vs  platform pydantic 2.13.4  (hard)
#     crewai regex~=2026.1.15         vs  platform regex 2026.6.28  (hard)
#     crewai portalocker~=2.7.0       vs  platform portalocker 3.2.0 (hard)
#     crewai opentelemetry-*~=1.42.0  vs  platform opentelemetry-sdk 1.43.0 (hard)
# The closure lives ONLY in the git-ignored sidecar venv
# (packages/ne-mcp/.crewai-venv), built the same way as packages/ne-eval/ragas_env/
# and packages/ne-mcp/langgraph_env/ via ne.envbuild.ensure_sidecar_venv.
#
# The customer's CrewAI agent (agent.py) consumes the platform's governed tools over
# MCP stdio via a DIRECT mcp-SDK client (CrewAI BaseTool proxies) — every tool call is
# C6-governed by construction because those are the ONLY tools it has.
#
# HARD RULE — NEVER add crewai-tools to this closure. Its MCPServerAdapter is NOT
# needed (we build the BaseTool->mcp-client proxy directly), and crewai-tools ships
# pymupdf (AGPL-3.0) in its BASE deps — adopting it at all is a copyleft event. The
# core loop only needs crewai's own base tool class (crewai.tools.BaseTool).
#
# --model mode needs NO extra pin: crewai bundles the openai SDK in its base closure,
# and --model targets a LOCAL OpenAI-compatible endpoint only (no frontier keys). The
# deterministic demo/live path performs ZERO model egress.
#
# mcp is declared explicitly because agent.py imports it directly (ClientSession /
# StdioServerParameters / stdio_client). crewai's own base pin mcp~=1.28.1 keeps the
# resolution on the 1.28.x line, matching the platform's own mcp>=1.28.1,<2 pin — same
# protocol line, no extra dependency beyond declaring it here.
#
# Compile with (NEVER hand-edit requirements.txt):
#   uv pip compile packages/ne-mcp/crewai_env/requirements.in --universal \
#       --python-version 3.12 --generate-hashes \
#       -o packages/ne-mcp/crewai_env/requirements.txt
crewai>=1.15.5,<2
mcp>=1.28.1,<2
